(:id "port/python/vt/widening" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/vtwiden_test.go: TestPythonVtWidening (19 manifest report rows: the three rows the engine widens, a1_arm_moved_width_as_a2, field_scalar_widen and map_key_widen, and the sibling field, arm, keyed, array-element and map-key refusals, with a completeness check that fails on any other manifest row the engine widens)" "internal/codegen/pythontable/vtwiden_test.go: TestPythonVtWideningNegativeControl/widen-ladder-off, /field-widened-not-counted, /arm-widened-not-counted, /map-widened-not-counted (each fault planted in a COPY of the emitted runtime)" "make python-vt-widening python-vt-widening-negative-control (make/python.mk); make/negative-controls.json: python-vt-widening") :tested-revision "e384eca618809f5e41eb31ed9a5110898a8a34ca" :note "2026-11-16: the variable-table widening read on the Python leg holds every manifest report row it uses, with no row skipped. Each row is read and written back under both pinned interpreters (CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2), accepted with the engine's widened counter and canonical form-1 bytes, or refused with the caller's LoadReport and input bytearray untouched; the three rows the engine widens are a1_arm_moved_width_as_a2 (one widened), field_scalar_widen (one) and map_key_widen (one), and every crossed signedness, narrowed kind and damaged array body beside them refuses. A fixed-declared root reads form 3 alone, which is the fixed-form row's (port/python/fixed/fixed-file-roundtrip); this cell asks the engine through the same declaration with the root variable, as the conformance harness does for a fixed root's framing rows, and still holds every row's declared-form verdict to reports.txt. The negative control turns the kind-pair ladder off, then stops the field, arm and map widened counters in a copy of the emitted runtime, and each guarded row goes red by name. Run on macOS arm64 at e384eca618809f5e41eb31ed9a5110898a8a34ca with SCHEMA_SLOW=1, -tags schema_leg_python, and make dist-python (the pinned CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 from the fleet SDK); make generated-current passed at the same head.")
